---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { sitePath } from '../../lib/siteUrl';
import StatusPill from '../../components/StatusPill.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Effect Studio"
  description="Browse, compare, tune, and apply curated editable effects in Varve without flattening vector or raster source content."
>
  <div class="container-custom">
    <main class="feature-page">
      <nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
        <a href={sitePath('/features')}>Features</a> / Effect Studio
      </nav>

      <header class="page-hero">
        <div class="eyebrow"><StatusPill status="available" /> <span>Curated editable effects</span></div>
        <h1>Preview the treatment. Keep the source.</h1>
        <p>
          Effect Studio turns a creative direction into an editable Object Filter recipe. Browse
          named treatments, compare the accepted state with the current candidate, adjust the
          controls, and decide when the result belongs in the document.
        </p>
      </header>

      <section class="feature-section feature-section--highlight" aria-labelledby="workflow-title">
        <p class="eyebrow">A deliberate workflow</p>
        <h2 id="workflow-title">See what will change before it becomes history.</h2>
        <div class="workflow-grid">
          <article><span>01</span><h3>Browse</h3><p>Search by creative family: mark making, optics, print, light, and more.</p></article>
          <article><span>02</span><h3>Compare</h3><p>Use Before, After, or a draggable split between the accepted state and current candidate.</p></article>
          <article><span>03</span><h3>Keep or cancel</h3><p>Keep adds one coherent recipe to the local undo history. Cancel removes only the preview-owned edits.</p></article>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="feature-section" aria-labelledby="treatments-title">
        <h2 id="treatments-title">Named treatments, editable internals.</h2>
        <p>
          A treatment is a discoverable recipe, not a flattened image. Reticulation, Halftone
          Pattern, Grain, Chromatic Bloom, and other recipes expose meaningful controls while
          preserving their derived Object Filter entries, order, masks, and blend behavior.
        </p>
        <div class="card-grid">
          <article><h3>Vector and raster</h3><p>Preview the rendered result for shapes, paths, text, groups, frames, and images while the original source remains editable.</p></article>
          <article><h3>One history step</h3><p>Apply, keep, cancel, and multi-selection application use the existing document transaction and undo system.</p></article>
          <article><h3>Explicit duplication</h3><p>Reapplying a treatment is an intentional Add another action, so an accidental second click does not silently duplicate the stack.</p></article>
          <article><h3>Inspect at scale</h3><p>Fit contains the complete preview; 100% and 200% show its encoded pixels at inspection scale, with drag-to-pan and a shared Center control for aligned comparisons.</p></article>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="feature-section feature-section--highlight" aria-labelledby="boundaries-title">
        <h2 id="boundaries-title">The right surface for the job.</h2>
        <dl class="surface-list">
          <div><dt>Effect Studio</dt><dd>Creative discovery and named, editable object-local recipes.</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Object Filters</dt><dd>Advanced per-effect order, opacity, blend, mask, and parameter editing.</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Image Tuning</dt><dd>Focused photographic corrections for selected image content.</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Adjustment Layers</dt><dd>Scoped corrections that intentionally cross object boundaries.</dd></div>
        </dl>
      </section>

      <section class="feature-section">
        <h2>Honest previews, local-first documents.</h2>
        <p>
          Studio previews use Varve's canonical rendering path and carry their identity, quality,
          warnings, and fallback state with the image. A provisional frame is disclosed while
          fonts or raster resources settle; it is never treated as the final accepted result.
          Documents store the editable recipe, not a preview bitmap.
        </p>
        <p><a href={sitePath('/docs/tools/effect-studio')}>Read the Effect Studio guide</a> or <a href={sitePath('/features/layer-effects')}>explore Layer Effects</a>.</p>
      </section>

      <div class="feature-cta">
        <h2>Make the look yours, then keep editing.</h2>
        <a href={sitePath('/download')} class="btn-default">Download Varve</a>
      </div>
    </main>
  </div>
</Layout>

<style>
  .feature-page { max-width: 860px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 3rem 0 5rem; }
  .breadcrumb { color: var(--text-secondary); font-size: .875rem; margin-bottom: 2.5rem; }
  .breadcrumb a, .feature-section a { color: var(--text-link); }
  .page-hero { max-width: 720px; margin-bottom: 4rem; }
  .eyebrow { align-items: center; color: var(--accent-primary); display: flex; font-size: .75rem; font-weight: 700; gap: .65rem; letter-spacing: .12em; text-transform: uppercase; }
  .page-hero h1 { color: var(--text-primary); font: 700 clamp(2.3rem, 6vw, 4rem)/1.05 var(--font-editorial); letter-spacing: -.025em; margin: 1rem 0; }
  .page-hero p, .feature-section p, .surface-list dd { color: var(--text-secondary); font-size: 1.05rem; line-height: 1.75; }
  .feature-section { margin: 0 0 4rem; }
  .feature-section h2 { color: var(--text-primary); font-size: clamp(1.6rem, 3vw, 2.3rem); margin: .5rem 0 1rem; }
  .feature-section h3 { color: var(--text-primary); margin: .65rem 0 .45rem; }
  .feature-section--highlight { background: var(--surface-card); border: 1px solid var(--border-default); border-radius: var(--website-radius-card); padding: clamp(1.5rem, 4vw, 3rem); }
  .workflow-grid, .card-grid { display: grid; gap: 1rem; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr)); margin-top: 1.75rem; }
  .workflow-grid article, .card-grid article { border: 1px solid var(--border-default); border-radius: var(--website-radius-surface); padding: 1rem; }
  .workflow-grid span { color: var(--accent-primary); font-size: .75rem; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
  .workflow-grid p, .card-grid p { font-size: .95rem; margin: 0; }
  .surface-list { display: grid; gap: .8rem; margin: 1.5rem 0 0; }
  .surface-list div { border-left: 2px solid var(--border-accent); padding-left: 1rem; }
  .surface-list dt { color: var(--text-primary); font-weight: 700; }
  .surface-list dd { margin: .2rem 0 0; }
  .feature-cta { border-top: 1px solid var(--border-default); padding-top: 2.5rem; text-align: center; }
  .feature-cta h2 { color: var(--text-primary); font-size: 1.35rem; margin-bottom: 1rem; }
  @media (max-width: 680px) { .workflow-grid, .card-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } .feature-page { padding-top: 2rem; } }
</style>
